===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*þurnuz||thorn, sloe}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*trnus}}, {{m|ine-pro|*tr̥nom}} < {{m|ine-pro|*(s)tern-||thorny bush, thorn}}, a variant of the base {{m|ine-pro|*(s)ter-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)terə-||rigid, stiff}}. Germanic cognates include {{cog|osx|thorn}} ({{cog|nds|Dorn}}, {{m|nds|Doorn}}), {{cog|nl|doorn}}, {{cog|goh|thorn}} ({{cog|de|Dorn}}), {{cog|non|þorn}} ({{cog|sv|törne}}), {{cog|got|𐌸𐌰𐌿𐍂𐌽𐌿𐍃}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|cu|трънъ|sc=Cyrs}} ({{cog|ru|тёрн||sloe, blackthorn}}, {{cog|sk|tŕň}}), {{cog|sa|तृण||grass}}.

